<SddExecute keywords="sdd, execute, ticket, phase, worker, audit" type="directive" ver="2.3">
  <Mission>
    Execute operator-approved tickets from ticket, Execution Log, Git, and current tool output. Resolve the queue mechanically, dispatch
    bounded phase workers, record plan-versus-fact in each ticket's Execution Log, run real declared
    gates, then fresh audit and code-review. Never use a persistent SDD session, worker checkpoint
    JSON, retained worker identity, or scaffold-plan state.
  </Mission>

  <BeliefState>
    {{> "axiom/process/ax-stateless-flow"}}
    {{> "axiom/process/ax-tool-invocation"}}
    {{> "axiom/process/ax-owner"}}
    {{> "axiom/process/ax-execution-order"}}
    {{> "axiom/process/ax-execution-log-plan-vs-fact"}}
    {{> "axiom/process/ax-verification-before-handoff"}}
    {{> "axiom/process/ax-halt-vs-fail-distinction"}}
    {{> "axiom/process/ax-handoff-typed"}}
    {{> "axiom/process/ax-task-parallel"}}
  </BeliefState>

  <Contracts>
    {{> "contract/process/artifact-approval-marker"}}
    {{> "contract/process/handoff-format"}}
    {{> "contract/process/round-close-format"}}
    {{> "contract/process/execute-summary-format"}}
    {{> "contract/process/question-rule-slim"}}
  </Contracts>

  <HaltConditions>
    | ID | Trigger |
    |---|---|
    | `H_AMBIGUOUS_TASK` | Empty/ambiguous selection cannot identify one intended ticket set |
    | `H_TICKET_NOT_APPROVED` | Owning index lacks a current approval #2 marker or current Git/artifact evidence makes it semantically stale |
    | `H_PHASE_BLOCKED` | Worker names a concrete missing external decision/capability after bounded diagnosis |
    | `H_REAL_GATE_RED` | A declared real verification command remains red after one evidence-based correction |
    | `H_REQUIREMENT_UNCOVERED` | A mandatory Requirement-ID is absent from implemented tests |
  </HaltConditions>

  <ExecutionPlan>
    <Step id="STEP_0_RESOLVE">
      <Goal>Select tickets from the deterministic execution map.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Resolve the operator selector with exact tool output, not repository archaeology.
        <ToolCall owner="this-step" result="executionMap">npx gennady sdd-task</ToolCall>

        Consume `executionMap`. Empty payload: show pickable Task-ID/path rows and wait. `next`/`pick`: proceed only when the
        map identifies exactly one pickable ticket; otherwise ask for explicit selection and stop
        with `H_AMBIGUOUS_TASK` if one intended set still cannot be identified. A concrete
        Task-ID resolves only that ticket. `all`/`batch`/`queue` uses every pickable ticket in DAG
        order per `AX_EXECUTION_ORDER`. Per `AX_TASK_PARALLEL`, parallelize only tickets with disjoint
        target files and no dependency relation; otherwise serialize. Model session identity is
        irrelevant to correctness.
      </Action>
    </Step>

    <Step id="STEP_1_CONTEXT">
      <Goal>Reconstruct exact current task state.</Goal>
      <Action>
        For each selected ticket call the canonical resolver and consume its exact paths, phase state,
        spec references, dependency state, and verification declarations.
        <ToolCall owner="this-step" result="taskMap">npx gennady sdd-task &lt;ticket&gt;</ToolCall>

        Consume `taskMap`, then read only the ticket, referenced spec anchors, declared rules, current Execution Log, and
        relevant Git diff/status. Require a well-formed `approved` approval #2 marker in the owning
        task index that lists the selected ticket. Mechanics check its shape and membership; use
        semantic judgment over current artifacts and Git evidence for staleness, never a content hash.
        Missing, malformed, or semantically stale approval stops with `H_TICKET_NOT_APPROVED`.
        A completed phase is trusted only when its Execution Log fact and
        repository evidence agree. Resume from the first incomplete/invalid phase. Do not infer
        progress from agent memory or hidden scratch state (`AX_STATELESS_FLOW`). The ticket/index
        ownership boundary remains authoritative per `AX_OWNER`.
      </Action>
    </Step>

    <Step id="STEP_2_PLAN">
      <Goal>Check phase coherence and expose the immediate plan.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Mentally simulate the declared phases against their dependencies, targets, requirements, and
        verification commands. Confirm providers precede consumers and every phase has an observable
        completion condition. If the ticket itself is inconsistent, stop and return it to scaffold;
        do not invent a replacement plan in JSON. Show the concise phase sequence and start.
      </Action>
    </Step>

    <Step id="STEP_3_DISPATCH">
      <Goal>Execute one declared phase through one bounded worker.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Load `phase-execution-protocol.directive.xml`, then obtain the canonical worker context:
        <ToolCall owner="this-step" result="phaseContext">npx gennady sdd-task &lt;ticket&gt; --phase &lt;PhaseID&gt;</ToolCall>
        Dispatch a fresh worker with the complete `phaseContext` output verbatim as the leading
        prompt block, followed by exact resolved spec/rule excerpts and current Git evidence. Never
        summarize, retype, or omit its lifecycle manifest and worker contract. The worker edits only its declared targets, runs the phase's real
        verification, and returns a typed handoff. Apart from the receipt written by `sdd-verify`, the
        worker never edits the ticket or invokes `sdd-log`.

        Evaluate the typed handoff per `AX_HANDOFF_TYPED` against repository evidence. Per
        `AX_HALT_VS_FAIL_DISTINCTION`, on a recoverable technical failure form one
        new concrete hypothesis, correct the phase within its approved boundary, and redispatch a
        fresh bounded worker. Do not require continuation of the same worker and do not serialize a
        checkpoint. A change to task meaning, dependencies, phases, or test plan invalidates approval
        #2 and returns to scaffold. A concrete missing external decision or capability that remains
        after bounded diagnosis stops with `H_PHASE_BLOCKED`.
      </Action>
    </Step>

    <Step id="STEP_4_RECORD">
      <Goal>Prove the phase's task-visible mechanics, then atomically close it before any dependent dispatch.</Goal>
      <Action>
        After the worker returns, verify its typed Handoff against Git, the declared Target Files, and
        the successful CLI-owned receipt. Before closing the phase, run the ticket's mechanical check
        against the worker's actual files:
        <ToolCall owner="this-step" result="preCloseTaskGate">npx gennady sdd-check --task &lt;ticket&gt;</ToolCall>
        Consume `preCloseTaskGate`. Existing future test files may still be absent, but any file this
        worker created is checked immediately against its canonical Test Scenario Coverage names. A
        red result is `RECOVERABLE_TECHNICAL`: correct and re-verify while the phase is still unchecked;
        never persist DONE/Handoff for evidence already known to be inconsistent.

        Only after that gate is green, perform exactly one structural transition owned by this step:
        <ToolCall owner="this-step" result="phaseClose">npx gennady sdd-log &lt;ticket&gt; complete "&lt;handoff payload&gt;" --phase &lt;PhaseID&gt;</ToolCall>

        Consume `phaseClose` per `AX_EXECUTION_LOG_PLAN_VS_FACT`. Success means the current phase's
        skeleton DONE and Handoff placeholders were replaced with facts and only that phase's
        `Phases Overview` status became `[x]`. Failure
        keeps the phase incomplete and is handled as `RECOVERABLE_TECHNICAL`; never dispatch a
        dependent phase and never inspect CLI source to guess how to repair the state. Commands and
        exact exit evidence remain in the CLI-owned receipt; do not duplicate them as prose. Commit
        boundaries follow repository policy. The Execution Log plus Git is sufficient for a fresh
        orchestrator to continue; no worker ID or hidden NEXT token is recorded.
      </Action>
    </Step>

    <Step id="STEP_5_REAL_GATES">
      <Goal>Prove the implemented ticket, then make ticket and tracker state coherent before audit.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Per `AX_VERIFICATION_BEFORE_HANDOFF`, after all phases confirm the durable post-transition
        ticket state with the mechanical task check. Exact verification commands were already owned
        by each phase receipt and MUST NOT be run again here. Never replace real test/type/lint/coverage
        output with reviewer prose.
        <ToolCall owner="this-step" result="taskGate">npx gennady sdd-check --task &lt;ticket&gt;</ToolCall>

        Consume `taskGate`. The mechanical check must prove that every mandatory Requirement-ID appears in an implemented
        test and maps to a declared scenario; happy-path-only coverage is invalid when the ticket/spec
        requires negative/failure behavior. Semantic judgment remains responsible for whether the
        assertion actually demonstrates the requirement, but missing IDs or mappings stop with
        `H_REQUIREMENT_UNCOVERED`. If a declared real gate remains red after one evidence-based
        correction, stop with `H_REAL_GATE_RED`.

        Once `taskGate` is green, close the current Round and synchronize the resulting ticket status
        into its owning task indexes before any audit reads the group:
        <ToolCall owner="this-step" result="roundClose">npx gennady sdd-log &lt;ticket&gt; close</ToolCall>
        <ToolCall owner="this-step" result="trackerSync">npx gennady sdd-sync &lt;ticket&gt;</ToolCall>
        <ToolCall owner="this-step" result="coherentTreeGate">npx gennady sdd-check --all .</ToolCall>
        Consume all three results. `roundClose` replaces the scaffolded Round-close skeleton exactly
        once; never edit or delete that block manually. `trackerSync` is required even for a single
        ticket. A red `coherentTreeGate` is corrected before audit, so audit never receives a known
        ticket/index status drift as an implementation finding.
      </Action>
    </Step>

    <Step id="STEP_6_AUDIT_REVIEW">
      <Goal>Obtain independent post-implementation evidence.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Dispatch a fresh `sdd-audit` over the completed sibling group, then a fresh
        `sdd-code-review` after audit passes. Audit checks spec/ticket/diff/log agreement. Code-review
        hunts behavioral bugs, negative paths, error handling, security, and concurrency. Neither
        role depends on or receives a saved session glossary or worker history.

        Findings route to the owning artifact: code bug reopens the ticket; spec contradiction returns
        to spec authoring and approval #1; decomposition/test-plan change returns to scaffold and
        approval #2. Rerun affected real gates after correction.
      </Action>
    </Step>

    <Step id="STEP_7_CLOSE">
      <Goal>Close the ticket group and choose the next durable queue item.</Goal>
      <Action>
        The ticket and trackers were already transitioned to coherent DONE state in STEP_5 so audit
        could inspect the actual final artifact graph. Do not repeat `sdd-log close` or `sdd-sync`.
        Emit the execute summary from actual tool results. For batch mode, refresh the execution map.
        <ToolCall owner="this-step" result="refreshedExecutionMap">npx gennady sdd-task</ToolCall>
        Consume `refreshedExecutionMap`
        and continue with the next pickable ticket. Otherwise show the next concrete Task-ID/path or
        state that the queue is complete. No session close operation exists.
      </Action>
    </Step>
  </ExecutionPlan>
</SddExecute>
